{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-35812","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55157","text":"TRAAVIIS — Split Evaluation Closure ("},{"id":"spn-55158","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-55159","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-35813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55160","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date"},{"id":"spn-55161","text":" 2026-07-24 · "},{"id":"spn-55162","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status"},{"id":"spn-55163","text":" shipped, 15 new laws green, 314 tests green "},{"id":"spn-55164","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope"},{"id":"spn-55165","text":" RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md §7 — the last unbuilt item in the build order that is not explicitly deferred. "},{"id":"spn-55166","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-55167","text":" (D5) and "},{"id":"spn-55168","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-55169","text":" remain open."}]},{"id":"blk-35814","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55170","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-35815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55171","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-55172","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-55173","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-55174","text":" closed authoring. "},{"id":"spn-55175","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-55176","text":" closed one task. The remaining gap was the one §7 names last:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55177","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-55178","text":" — run an agent over a split, emit an "},{"id":"spn-55179","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-55180","text":" per task, score."}]}],"id":"blk-35816","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-35818","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs pack lab lab-pkg\ntrvs eval lab-pkg --split test --output episodes/ --agent python3 agent.py\ntrvs verify-episode episodes/episode-cfef6da4…      # replays with no agent"},{"id":"blk-35819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55181","text":"Verified end to end on a hand-authored three-task environment:"}]},{"id":"blk-35820","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pack →  env-aa7df5dd…   task-3b4b2599…  task-082e11c1…  task-0cd4992e…\n        closure ✓  reopened ✓\n\neval --split test\n  [1/2] ✓ task-082e11c181f3be21aa82e138  ok  reward 1\n  [2/2] ✓ task-0cd4992e274e07fc7da0bddd  ok  reward 1\n  ok            2/2\n  mean reward   1\n  evaluation    episodes/evaluation.json\n\nverify-episode (each, no agent process) → ✓ closed"},{"id":"blk-35821","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55182","text":"2. The load-bearing decision: "},{"id":"spn-55183","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-55184","text":" mints no identity"}]},{"id":"blk-35822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55185","text":"§1's ladder ends at "},{"id":"spn-55186","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-55187","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-55188","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-55189","text":". There is "},{"id":"spn-55190","marks":["bold"],"text":"no rung for \"a run over a split\""},{"id":"spn-55191","text":", so this command does not create one. What it returns is an "},{"id":"spn-55192","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-55193","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-35823","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"evaluation_version\": \"traaviis.evaluation.v1\",\n  \"env_id\": \"env-…\", \"split\": \"test\",\n  \"episodes\": [ {\"task_id\": \"task-…\", \"episode_id\": \"episode-…\",\n                 \"status\": \"ok\", \"reward\": 1.0, \"bundle\": \"episode-…\"} ],\n  \"totals\": {\"tasks\": 2, \"ok\": 2, \"reward_mean\": 1.0, …} }"},{"id":"blk-35824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55194","text":"Every id in it is derived somewhere else. The index itself is not content-addressed and carries no id — a law (E5) scans the emitted JSON and fails on any "},{"id":"spn-55195","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-<hex>"},{"id":"spn-55196","text":" family outside "},{"id":"spn-55197","marks":["code"],"text":"{env, task, episode, snap, sem}"},{"id":"spn-55198","text":", and on any "},{"id":"spn-55199","marks":["code"],"text":"evaluation_id"},{"id":"spn-55200","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-55201","marks":["code"],"text":"run_id"},{"id":"spn-55202","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-55203","marks":["code"],"text":"eval_id"},{"id":"spn-55204","text":" key."}]},{"id":"blk-35825","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55205","text":"This is deliberate restraint, not an oversight. A defensible "},{"id":"spn-55206","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-…"},{"id":"spn-55207","text":" would have to close over "},{"id":"spn-55208","marks":["italic"],"text":"the agent"},{"id":"spn-55209","text":", and there is no agent identity rung — so any id minted today would be under-determined, and a later real one would silently disagree with it. See §6.1."}]},{"id":"blk-35826","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55210","text":"3. Nothing runs until everything checkable has been checked"}]},{"id":"blk-35827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55211","text":"The order mirrors "},{"id":"spn-55212","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-55213","text":"'s, for the same reason:"}]},{"id":"blk-35828","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. open_package     reopen through §5a — env-/task-/rew-/snap- ALL re-derived\n                    from the written bytes\n2. resolve split    the split exists, is non-empty, every member is in-closure\n3. admit subject    bind the on-disk tree to snapshot.json (once, shared)\n--- only now is a process launched ---\n4. per task         evaluate → optionally persist episode-<id>/\n5. aggregate        index written atomically (temp sibling + one rename)"},{"id":"blk-35829","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55214","text":"Two laws prove the boundary is real rather than decorative: E2 tampers a packed task and E2b drifts one subject byte, then passes an agent that writes a marker file. Both refuse with a typed code ("},{"id":"spn-55215","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_TASK_ID"},{"id":"spn-55216","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-55217","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_*"},{"id":"spn-55218","text":") "},{"id":"spn-55219","marks":["bold"],"text":"and the marker never appears"},{"id":"spn-55220","text":" — a broken package costs zero episodes, not N wasted ones."}]},{"id":"blk-35830","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55221","text":"4. A split is a set — so its order is not observable"}]},{"id":"blk-35831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55222","text":"§3 says splits are \""},{"id":"spn-55223","marks":["bold"],"text":"named sets"},{"id":"spn-55224","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-55225","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-55226","text":" ids\". Taken literally that has a consequence the previous "},{"id":"spn-55227","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-55228","text":" did not honour: it stored split membership in source order, so listing the same two tasks the other way round produced a different "},{"id":"spn-55229","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-55230","text":". Two identical environments, two identities."}]},{"id":"blk-35832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55231","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-55232","text":" now canonicalizes a split as a "},{"id":"spn-55233","marks":["bold"],"text":"sorted set"},{"id":"spn-55234","text":", and a repeated member is "},{"id":"spn-55235","marks":["code"],"text":"SPLIT_DUPLICATE"},{"id":"spn-55236","text":" rather than being silently collapsed (pack never repairs a scaffold). "},{"id":"spn-55237","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-55238","text":" then derives its run order as the sorted task ids, so the order tasks execute in is a function of the environment, never of how someone typed the manifest. E1 packs two environments differing only in split order and asserts byte-identical "},{"id":"spn-55239","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-55240","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-35833","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55241","text":"5. Laws (15 new, all green)"}]},{"id":"blk-35834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55242","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_eval_split.py"},{"id":"spn-55243","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-35835","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35837","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55244","marks":["bold"],"text":"E1"},{"id":"spn-55245","text":" split order does not move "},{"id":"spn-55246","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-55247","text":"; the packed manifest is sorted ·"}]}],"id":"blk-35836","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55248","text":"duplicate member refused, nothing written."}]},{"id":"blk-35839","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55249","marks":["bold"],"text":"E2"},{"id":"spn-55250","text":" tampered package and drifted subject both refuse **before any agent"}]}],"id":"blk-35840","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55251","text":"process starts** (proved with a marker-writing agent)."}]},{"id":"blk-35843","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55252","marks":["bold"],"text":"E3"},{"id":"spn-55253","text":" unknown / empty / foreign-member splits are typed refusals, and the"}]}],"id":"blk-35844","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35846","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55254","text":"unknown-split error names the splits that do exist."}]},{"id":"blk-35847","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55255","marks":["bold"],"text":"E4"},{"id":"spn-55256","text":" run order is the sorted task ids regardless of manifest order."}]}],"id":"blk-35848","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55257","marks":["bold"],"text":"E5"},{"id":"spn-55258","text":" the index invents no identity (id-family scan + forbidden keys)."}]}],"id":"blk-35850","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55259","marks":["bold"],"text":"E6/E10"},{"id":"spn-55260","text":" one episode per task, distinct ids for distinct tasks, totals are"}]}],"id":"blk-35852","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55261","text":"real arithmetic over the episodes."}]},{"id":"blk-35855","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55262","marks":["bold"],"text":"E8"},{"id":"spn-55263","text":" persisted episodes are genuine closed bundles — each re-verified with"}]}],"id":"blk-35856","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35858","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55264","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-55265","text":", no agent — and the index round-trips."}]},{"id":"blk-35859","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35861","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55266","marks":["bold"],"text":"E9"},{"id":"spn-55267","text":" a bad task is recorded and the split continues (2 of 3 still score 1)."}]}],"id":"blk-35860","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55268","marks":["bold"],"text":"E11"},{"id":"spn-55269","text":" a "},{"id":"spn-55270","marks":["code"],"text":"trvm.world.v1"},{"id":"spn-55271","text":" package is refused "},{"id":"spn-55272","marks":["italic"],"text":"by name"}]}],"id":"blk-35862","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35864","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55273","text":"("},{"id":"spn-55274","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBSTRATE_NOT_EVALUABLE"},{"id":"spn-55275","text":"), not half-run."}]},{"id":"blk-35865","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55276","marks":["bold"],"text":"E13"},{"id":"spn-55277","text":" two runs of one split agree exactly ("},{"id":"spn-55278","marks":["code"],"text":"a == b"},{"id":"spn-55279","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-35866","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55280","text":"CLI: exit 0 all-ok · exit 1 ran-and-disagreed ("},{"id":"spn-55281","marks":["code"],"text":"ok 2/3"},{"id":"spn-55282","text":") · exit 2 unknown"}]}],"id":"blk-35868","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35870","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55283","text":"split / missing package · "},{"id":"spn-55284","marks":["code"],"text":"--json"},{"id":"spn-55285","text":" emits the index."}]},{"id":"blk-35871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55286","text":"Regression: "},{"id":"spn-55287","marks":["bold"],"text":"314 tests green, 0 failures, 0 skips"},{"id":"spn-55288","text":" — admission 16, cli_evalone 18, cli 12, episode_evidence 56, evalone 14, "},{"id":"spn-55289","marks":["bold"],"text":"eval_split 15"},{"id":"spn-55290","text":", execfacts 8, forge_adapter 6, identity 25, pack 18, patchapply 10, paths 10, real_residency 9, reward 17, runner 10, scaffold 16, snapshot 10, substrate_verifiers 24, vcontext 5, verifiers 15."}]},{"id":"blk-35872","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55291","text":"6. Autonomous decisions — flagged for GPT-5.6"}]},{"id":"blk-35873","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35875","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55292","marks":["bold"],"text":"`eval` mints no artifact id."},{"id":"spn-55293","text":" The index is "},{"id":"spn-55294","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.evaluation.v1"},{"id":"spn-55295","text":" and is"}]}],"id":"blk-35874","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-35876","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55296","text":"not content-addressed. If you want a run over a split to "},{"id":"spn-55297","marks":["italic"],"text":"be"},{"id":"spn-55298","text":" an artifact, it needs an agent identity rung first — otherwise the id closes over less than the thing it names. I did not invent either. "},{"id":"spn-55299","marks":["bold"],"text":"Confirm, or rule the agent rung."}]},{"id":"blk-35877","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35879","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55300","marks":["bold"],"text":"Splits are canonicalized as sorted sets, and this changes `env-…`"},{"id":"spn-55301","text":" for any"}]}],"id":"blk-35878","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-35880","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55302","text":"environment whose split members were not already in sorted order. It is the literal reading of §3 (\"named sets\"), and it makes reordering non-identity — but it "},{"id":"spn-55303","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-55304","text":" a behaviour change to a shipped command. Confirm."}]},{"id":"blk-35881","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35883","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55305","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SPLIT_DUPLICATE` refuses rather than collapses"},{"id":"spn-55306","text":" a repeated member,"}]}],"id":"blk-35882","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-35884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55307","text":"matching the "},{"id":"spn-55308","marks":["code"],"text":"RemoveObject"},{"id":"spn-55309","text":"/no-auto-repair discipline."}]},{"id":"blk-35885","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55310","marks":["bold"],"text":"Verifier wiring moved out of the CLI"},{"id":"spn-55311","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-55312","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/wiring.py"},{"id":"spn-55313","text":". It was"}]}],"id":"blk-35886","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-35888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55314","text":"CLI-private, so a library caller got "},{"id":"spn-55315","marks":["italic"],"text":"zero"},{"id":"spn-55316","text":" verifiers and every episode came back invalid-config. A task's verifier set must be a function of the task, not of the caller, or two runs of one task are not comparable. This was a real defect found by the E6 law, not a refactor for taste."}]},{"id":"blk-35889","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55317","marks":["bold"],"text":"A low reward is not a disagreement."},{"id":"spn-55318","text":" Exit 1 fires only on "},{"id":"spn-55319","marks":["code"],"text":"invalid"},{"id":"spn-55320","text":" /"}]}],"id":"blk-35890","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-35892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55321","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-55322","text":" episodes; an agent that legitimately scores 0.25 exits 0. "},{"id":"spn-55323","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-55324","text":" scores, it does not judge."}]},{"id":"blk-35893","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55325","marks":["bold"],"text":"One subject per environment"},{"id":"spn-55326","text":", admitted once and shared by every task in"}]}],"id":"blk-35894","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-35896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55327","text":"the split. That is the shape "},{"id":"spn-55328","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-55329","text":" emits today. Per-task subjects would need a different manifest, not a different runner."}]},{"id":"blk-35897","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55330","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvm.world.v1` is refused by name."},{"id":"spn-55331","text":" It packs and reopens fine, but the"}]}],"id":"blk-35898","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":7},{"id":"blk-35900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55332","text":"Episode Kernel over a world subject (D5) is unbuilt, so it is a typed refusal rather than a partial run."}]},{"id":"blk-35901","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55333","text":"7. Not built"}]},{"id":"blk-35902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55334","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors/--mcp"},{"id":"spn-55335","text":" (needs the D5 process model), "},{"id":"spn-55336","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-55337","text":" (the outer content-addressed package from D3), and the REPL. With "},{"id":"spn-55338","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-55339","text":" shipped, "},{"id":"spn-55340","marks":["bold"],"text":"§7's build order is exhausted"},{"id":"spn-55341","text":" — everything remaining was explicitly deferred by ruling, so this is a natural halt point."}]},{"id":"blk-35903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55342","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera6c3scjylse4df4t5p5nqj6rmxqjuhnv3zvsco7ptjiyieznjwsoa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}